      "source": "https://sykesboro.org/history/",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The borough lies in the valley of Stump Creek, a southward‑flowing tributary that joins Mahoning Creek before reaching the Allegheny River.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        9
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sykesville%2C_Pennsylvania",
      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Route 119 runs through Sykesville’s center, leading six miles northeast to DuBois and thirteen miles southwest to Punxsutawney.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
